1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:06,000
In Resident Evil, Raccoon City has one night left, and you live there.

2
00:00:06,450 --> 00:00:14,130
No badge. No gun. No Umbrella ID card. Just you, a car with half a tank, and snow coming down.

3
00:00:14,583 --> 00:00:18,583
Somewhere in this night is the exact moment you had to leave.

4
00:00:19,050 --> 00:00:23,850
By the end, you'll know when it was, and why almost nobody leaves in time.

5
00:00:24,317 --> 00:00:26,317
Because real cities have been here before.

6
00:00:26,783 --> 00:00:33,583
In 1979, a cloud of anthrax spores escaped from a military lab in the Soviet city of Sverdlovsk.

7
00:00:34,050 --> 00:00:38,690
Dozens of people died, almost all of them along one narrow strip of the city.

8
00:00:39,150 --> 00:00:42,190
The government told everyone it was contaminated meat.

9
00:00:42,650 --> 00:00:46,570
Remember that. Raccoon City gets a cover story too.

10
00:00:47,017 --> 00:00:52,457
The new Resident Evil, directed by Zach Cregger, takes place over one snowy night in the mountains of Colorado.

11
00:00:52,917 --> 00:00:58,197
The director says it happens in 2026, alongside the events of Resident Evil 2.

12
00:00:58,650 --> 00:01:01,930
The film follows a medical courier driving in from outside.

13
00:01:02,383 --> 00:01:07,103
It barely shows the people who actually live there. So this story follows you.

14
00:01:07,550 --> 00:01:16,350
For the city and the night, we'll use the film. For what the authorities do, the games. And for how people really behave, real disasters.

15
00:01:18,167 --> 00:01:24,727
It's 9:40 on a winter night. Dinner's done. The snow has been falling since the afternoon.

16
00:01:25,183 --> 00:01:30,143
Your phone buzzes. A friend downtown: "Something's going on near the hospital."

17
00:01:30,583 --> 00:01:35,223
Then a local news alert: a disturbance downtown. Possibly a riot.

18
00:01:35,683 --> 00:01:44,003
In the games, that's exactly how the city first hears about it. First a riot. Later, a radiation spill. Then a skin disease.

19
00:01:44,450 --> 00:01:50,050
And in the games, the hospital had been seeing patients for days, with something locals called the "cannibal disease."

20
00:01:50,517 --> 00:01:53,717
But tonight, all you know is the word riot.

21
00:01:54,183 --> 00:01:56,583
So you do what almost everyone does.

22
00:01:57,050 --> 00:01:58,970
You look for more information.

23
00:01:59,417 --> 00:02:03,577
You refresh the news. You text three people. You turn on the TV.

24
00:02:04,017 --> 00:02:07,777
Disaster researchers have a name for this. They call it milling.

25
00:02:08,217 --> 00:02:16,217
On 9/11, after the first plane hit the North Tower, people below the impact zone waited a median of three minutes before starting down the stairs.

26
00:02:16,650 --> 00:02:18,810
With a fire burning above them.

27
00:02:19,250 --> 00:02:25,490
And investigators found that the more people stopped to talk and look for information, the longer they took to leave.

28
00:02:25,950 --> 00:02:31,070
You have the whole internet in your hand. Your milling can last all night.

29
00:02:31,517 --> 00:02:35,117
Researchers found something else, and it's not what the movies show.

30
00:02:35,583 --> 00:02:41,743
In real disasters, mass panic is rare. Most people stay calm, and they help each other.

31
00:02:42,183 --> 00:02:43,863
That's good news for the world.

32
00:02:44,317 --> 00:02:47,917
It's bad news for you tonight. Because calm people wait.

33
00:02:48,383 --> 00:02:51,503
At 10:15, your friend downtown stops answering.

34
00:02:53,300 --> 00:02:55,700
At 10:30, you decide to leave.

35
00:02:56,150 --> 00:03:01,270
First you try to call your family. The call doesn't go through. Neither does the next one.

36
00:03:01,717 --> 00:03:03,477
That part is real too.

37
00:03:03,917 --> 00:03:09,917
In 2011, an earthquake shook Virginia and the East Coast. No cell towers came down.

38
00:03:10,383 --> 00:03:14,863
But so many people called at once that even emergency calls got stuck in the network.

39
00:03:15,317 --> 00:03:22,517
A federal official later admitted that even the priority system for emergency workers failed, because the network was flooded with texts.

40
00:03:22,983 --> 00:03:25,543
So you stop calling, and you pack.

41
00:03:25,983 --> 00:03:31,743
Water. A jacket. Painkillers. Your charger. The car keys.

42
00:03:32,183 --> 00:03:36,583
And from the kitchen drawer, the old paper map of the county you never thought you'd use.

43
00:03:37,050 --> 00:03:40,170
Raccoon City is surrounded by the Arklay Mountains.

44
00:03:40,617 --> 00:03:46,937
Which leaves three ways out. The highway. The tunnel. Or the mountains, on foot.

45
00:03:47,383 --> 00:03:51,303
You pick the highway. Everyone picks the highway.

46
00:03:53,100 --> 00:03:57,020
By 11:15, you've moved two miles in forty minutes.

47
00:03:57,483 --> 00:04:00,843
The line of red tail lights goes all the way up the hill.

48
00:04:01,283 --> 00:04:04,563
Real evacuations look exactly like this.

49
00:04:05,017 --> 00:04:12,777
In 2005, as Hurricane Rita approached Texas, the official hurricane report says more than two million people may have fled.

50
00:04:13,217 --> 00:04:17,697
Some drives from Houston to Dallas, normally about four hours, took twenty.

51
00:04:18,150 --> 00:04:21,430
The storm itself killed seven people directly.

52
00:04:21,883 --> 00:04:28,283
On the road, a single bus of elderly evacuees caught fire, and more than twenty of them died.

53
00:04:28,750 --> 00:04:33,470
In Texas, the evacuation killed more people than the wind and the water.

54
00:04:33,917 --> 00:04:37,197
Now put that traffic in a city where something is biting people.

55
00:04:37,650 --> 00:04:42,770
Up ahead, car doors open. People are running back down the hill, between the cars.

56
00:04:43,217 --> 00:04:47,377
You don't wait to find out why. You turn around on the shoulder.

57
00:04:47,817 --> 00:04:52,457
If you want more nights like this one, that's what the subscribe button is for. Now, the tunnel.

58
00:04:54,267 --> 00:04:58,427
The tunnel on the old mountain road is the way the film's courier comes into town.

59
00:04:58,883 --> 00:05:05,123
In the film, it's choked with abandoned cars, and at the far end, a stalled RV blocks the way.

60
00:05:05,583 --> 00:05:11,903
You don't get that far. The cars inside are empty. Doors open. Engines off.

61
00:05:12,350 --> 00:05:15,550
And in the dark between them, something moves.

62
00:05:16,017 --> 00:05:18,737
This is when you need to understand what you're dealing with.

63
00:05:19,183 --> 00:05:23,103
Cregger's infected aren't the slow zombies of old movies.

64
00:05:23,550 --> 00:05:28,910
The infection changes bodies. Some grow tentacles. Some fuse together.

65
00:05:29,350 --> 00:05:33,990
And it spreads through a bite. In the film, one bite is enough to start the change.

66
00:05:34,450 --> 00:05:41,410
In the real world, there is one disease that spreads through bites and changes how its victims behave. Rabies.

67
00:05:41,850 --> 00:05:47,450
Once symptoms appear, the World Health Organization says it is fatal in one hundred percent of cases.

68
00:05:47,917 --> 00:05:52,077
But it's slow. Usually two to three months from the bite to the first symptoms.

69
00:05:52,517 --> 00:05:56,277
In Raccoon City, the film suggests it's a matter of hours.

70
00:05:56,717 --> 00:06:00,717
So tonight the rule is simple: nobody gets close enough to bite you.

71
00:06:01,183 --> 00:06:03,823
You back out of the tunnel. Two ways out are gone.

72
00:06:05,633 --> 00:06:11,633
You drive back toward town, because that's where the fuel is, and the people, and maybe some answers.

73
00:06:12,083 --> 00:06:16,563
Downtown, the streetlights are still on. That's almost the worst part.

74
00:06:17,017 --> 00:06:21,577
Near the hospital, people are falling from the rooftops, and not getting up.

75
00:06:22,017 --> 00:06:26,817
And everywhere you look, there's the same red and white logo. Umbrella.

76
00:06:27,283 --> 00:06:31,203
In the games, Umbrella is the biggest employer in Raccoon City.

77
00:06:31,650 --> 00:06:40,690
In the film, the story is that Umbrella was building a serum for the US government, something that makes living things evolve fast, and there was an accident in the lab.

78
00:06:41,150 --> 00:06:44,510
A secret lab. An accident. A city downwind.

79
00:06:44,950 --> 00:06:46,710
That's Sverdlovsk again.

80
00:06:47,150 --> 00:06:55,070
When scientists finally studied it, in 1994, they found that most victims had lived or worked in a narrow strip running south from the military lab.

81
00:06:55,517 --> 00:07:00,317
Farther along that same line, livestock died of anthrax too.

82
00:07:00,783 --> 00:07:04,543
The strip followed the wind that had been blowing just before the outbreak.

83
00:07:04,983 --> 00:07:06,983
The meat story was false.

84
00:07:07,450 --> 00:07:12,090
Which means the people in charge of Raccoon City probably know exactly what this is.

85
00:07:12,550 --> 00:07:16,550
And they have a plan for the city. It isn't the one you'd hope for.

86
00:07:18,367 --> 00:07:23,967
By two in the morning, the radio has new instructions: stay indoors, or go to an evacuation point.

87
00:07:24,417 --> 00:07:30,497
In the games, that's what the authorities do. Roadblocks, evacuation points, and then the army.

88
00:07:30,950 --> 00:07:36,150
And in the games, the soldiers at the edge of the city have orders to shoot anyone who tries to cross the line.

89
00:07:36,617 --> 00:07:39,257
That sounds like something only fiction would do.

90
00:07:39,717 --> 00:07:47,557
In 2014, during the Ebola epidemic, Liberia sealed off West Point, a neighborhood of Monrovia with about eighty thousand people.

91
00:07:48,017 --> 00:07:52,897
Barbed wire. Soldiers. A quarantine meant to last twenty-one days.

92
00:07:53,350 --> 00:07:57,270
On the first day, people tried to push through, and soldiers opened fire.

93
00:07:57,717 --> 00:08:01,717
A sixteen-year-old named Shacki Kamara was shot in the legs.

94
00:08:02,183 --> 00:08:07,383
He lay in the street, bleeding, for at least twenty minutes before anyone took him to a hospital. He died.

95
00:08:07,850 --> 00:08:11,050
The quarantine was lifted after about ten days.

96
00:08:11,517 --> 00:08:16,637
So the edge of the city isn't safe either. Not for the infected, and not for you.

97
00:08:17,083 --> 00:08:21,483
Half a tank. Phone at twenty percent. Two choices left.

98
00:08:21,950 --> 00:08:25,950
One: the evacuation point downtown, where the helicopters land.

99
00:08:26,417 --> 00:08:31,937
Two: leave the car, take the map, and walk out over the mountains, in the snow, in the dark.

100
00:08:32,383 --> 00:08:36,543
Helicopter, or mountains? Tell me in the comments which one you'd pick.

101
00:08:36,983 --> 00:08:39,303
Here's what happens if you pick the helicopter.

102
00:08:41,100 --> 00:08:45,980
The crowd at the evacuation point is calm. Mostly. Just like the research says.

103
00:08:46,417 --> 00:08:49,617
People share blankets. Someone hands out water.

104
00:08:50,083 --> 00:08:54,963
In front of you in line, a man has his forearm wrapped in a bloody towel.

105
00:08:55,417 --> 00:08:58,777
He says he cut himself on glass. Maybe he did.

106
00:08:59,217 --> 00:09:05,057
In the games, an evacuation helicopter full of refugees went down after some of the people on board turned.

107
00:09:05,517 --> 00:09:10,237
A crowd is where help is. It's also where a bite finds its next victim.

108
00:09:10,683 --> 00:09:13,963
You remember the rule. Nobody gets close enough to bite you.

109
00:09:14,417 --> 00:09:16,257
You step out of the line.

110
00:09:16,717 --> 00:09:21,437
You leave the car, you take the map, and you walk toward the mountains.

111
00:09:23,233 --> 00:09:26,513
The road up is dark, and the snow is up to your knees.

112
00:09:26,950 --> 00:09:33,270
In the film, this is Arklay County: farms, pine forest, and a road where a woman steps out of the trees.

113
00:09:33,717 --> 00:09:42,757
In the games, this forest is where it all began: months earlier, hikers were found dead in the Arklay Mountains, and the police blamed a cannibal cult.

114
00:09:43,217 --> 00:09:47,537
You walk past a farmhouse with its door wide open. You don't go in.

115
00:09:47,983 --> 00:09:52,303
At 4:30, your phone dies. Not from the battery. From the cold.

116
00:09:52,750 --> 00:09:58,910
Apple itself warns that very cold conditions can shorten an iPhone's battery life, and even make it turn off.

117
00:09:59,350 --> 00:10:02,790
So now it's just you, a flashlight, and a paper map.

118
00:10:03,250 --> 00:10:06,050
The map shows an old fire road over the ridge.

119
00:10:06,517 --> 00:10:10,677
You follow it, one step at a time, until the sky turns grey.

120
00:10:12,467 --> 00:10:14,387
At the top of the ridge, you look back.

121
00:10:14,850 --> 00:10:20,130
Raccoon City is down there, under the snow. A few fires. A few lights still on.

122
00:10:20,583 --> 00:10:24,663
The moment you had to leave wasn't two in the morning. It wasn't 10:30.

123
00:10:25,117 --> 00:10:29,197
It was 9:40. The first alert. The word riot.

124
00:10:29,650 --> 00:10:36,770
Every hour after that, the way out got smaller. First the phones. Then the highway. Then the tunnel. Then the line.

125
00:10:37,217 --> 00:10:42,737
And you waited for the same reason almost everyone waits. You were looking for more information.

126
00:10:43,183 --> 00:10:49,583
When Wuhan was locked down in 2020, the announcement came at two in the morning. The city closed at ten.

127
00:10:50,050 --> 00:10:53,410
Eight hours' notice, for a city of eleven million people.

128
00:10:53,850 --> 00:10:57,770
In the games, Raccoon City never even got the real announcement.

129
00:10:58,217 --> 00:11:02,617
You made it out because, at two in the morning, you stopped waiting for someone to tell you what to do.

130
00:11:04,433 --> 00:11:07,873
As the sun comes up, you hear helicopters over the city.

131
00:11:08,317 --> 00:11:13,757
In the film, that's how the night ends: helicopters arriving over Raccoon City.

132
00:11:14,217 --> 00:11:21,257
In the games, a few days later, the government ends the city for good: one missile, at sunrise, on the first of October.

133
00:11:21,717 --> 00:11:24,997
The games say more than a hundred thousand people died.

134
00:11:25,450 --> 00:11:27,130
And the official story?

135
00:11:27,583 --> 00:11:31,183
In Sverdlovsk, the truth stayed buried for thirteen years.

136
00:11:31,650 --> 00:11:37,650
In 1992, Boris Yeltsin, by then the president of Russia, admitted that the military was to blame.

137
00:11:38,117 --> 00:11:43,157
In 1979, he had been the Communist Party boss in Sverdlovsk.

138
00:11:43,617 --> 00:11:48,897
So when the news finally talks about Raccoon City, don't expect to hear the word Umbrella.

139
00:11:49,350 --> 00:11:54,710
Down below, one of the helicopters turns. Its searchlight starts to climb the ridge, toward you.

140
00:11:55,150 --> 00:11:56,750
You raise your arm.

141
00:11:57,217 --> 00:12:02,817
In Raccoon City, that has always been the question: are they here to get you out, or to keep you in?
